(2586353, 354718, 8891, '<td valign="top">Thanks, Ursula and Neil!  And thank for all the great comments during the challenge!<br/> <br/>Neil: I opened a blank file in PSElements 3.0. I put up a quater inch grid to use as a template. I clicked on the backgrond color icon and brought up the Color Picker and chose several different hues of green. I selected one 1/4" vertical space of the grid with the Rectangular Marquee tool and then filled the selected area with Paint Bucket tool. Repeated for about a dozen different colors. Then I copy and pasted the inital set across the background and, when completed, merged down each set. The I sharpened it a bit to give a better definition between the colors. The curves were made with the Shear filter. Here is a downsized version of the background: <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=358792" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/8891/thumb/358792.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/8891/thumb/358792.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/8891/thumb/358792.jpg"/></a><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-07-05 02:25:47.</i></td>', 'Thanks, Ursula and Neil!  And thank for all the great comments during the challenge! Neil: I opened a blank file in PSElements 3.0. I put up a quater inch grid to use as a template. I clicked on the backgrond color icon and brought up the Color Picker and chose several different hues of green. I selected one 1/4" vertical space of the grid with the Rectangular Marquee tool and then filled the selected area with Paint Bucket tool. Repeated for about a dozen different colors. Then I copy and pasted the inital set across the background and, when completed, merged down each set. The I sharpened it a bit to give a better definition between the colors. The curves were made with the Shear filter. Here is a downsized version of the background: ', '2006-07-05 03:25:03.000000', '2006-07-05 03:25:47.000000', 0),
