(2612082, 353977, 7969, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the CC. <br/>I like your image while not shouting wow it is clean, simple, clear and to the point. I like the black background as it really serves to give punch to the subject. I do think if the bulb were on a bit more of an angle it would give the image a little stronger compostion.  Also I would of tried to get rid of that highlight on the bulb it self. <br/>I like that it is not cluttered.  <br/>Well done, lynn</td>', 'Greetings from the CC. I like your image while not shouting wow it is clean, simple, clear and to the point. I like the black background as it really serves to give punch to the subject. I do think if the bulb were on a bit more of an angle it would give the image a little stronger compostion.  Also I would of tried to get rid of that highlight on the bulb it self. I like that it is not cluttered.  Well done, lynn', '2006-07-11 21:11:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(2612093, 354554, 7969, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the CC, well this gets points I guess for experimental and creative. And knowing that you have been around here a long time, I suspect you knew this would not score high on dpc.  I actually think this image is interesting, I think it may have worked much better tho as a vertical crop, partly cuz it is such a busy image it would of helped to focus the eye, in at least my opinion on the more interesting ''middle'' part. <br/>I suspect not possible but had you been able to get this a bit sharper, it would of looked IMHO like a jewel.<br/>I also would like to see the ''white version''.  <br/> <br/>Hope that helps1<br/>Lynn</td>', 'Greetings from the CC, well this gets points I guess for experimental and creative. And knowing that you have been around here a long time, I suspect you knew this would not score high on dpc.  I actually think this image is interesting, I think it may have worked much better tho as a vertical crop, partly cuz it is such a busy image it would of helped to focus the eye, in at least my opinion on the more interesting ''middle'' part. I suspect not possible but had you been able to get this a bit sharper, it would of looked IMHO like a jewel.I also would like to see the ''white version''.   Hope that helps1Lynn', '2006-07-11 21:17:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(2612100, 353456, 14476, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings form the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>Love it!<br/> <br/>YOu have an original take on the Challenge that was quite well rewarded by our voters.  Composition is excellent; technique, as far as I can tell, is just fine.  My first impression on seeing the shot - and this is important, I suppose for our fast voters - was that the shot was a little hot.<br/> <br/>But then, I stopped to think, "well, yeah!  It''s likely to be a little hot isn''t it! How many degrees is that furnace, anyhow?"<br/> <br/>So, the only offering I have to make is one you probably have already thought of:  Bracket those shots.  Try different ISOs, try different apertures, etc. etc. Experiment.<br/> <br/>Oh, heck.  You''re doing fine. Keep up the good work.<br/> <br/>Alice</td>', 'Greetings form the Critique Club  Love it! YOu have an original take on the Challenge that was quite well rewarded by our voters.  Composition is excellent; technique, as far as I can tell, is just fine.  My first impression on seeing the shot - and this is important, I suppose for our fast voters - was that the shot was a little hot. But then, I stopped to think, "well, yeah!  It''s likely to be a little hot isn''t it! How many degrees is that furnace, anyhow?" So, the only offering I have to make is one you probably have already thought of:  Bracket those shots.  Try different ISOs, try different apertures, etc. etc. Experiment. Oh, heck.  You''re doing fine. Keep up the good work. Alice', '2006-07-11 21:22:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(2612127, 354126, 9906, '<td valign="top">From the Critique Club:<br/> <br/>First of all, let me say welcome back!  Don''t know what kept ya out of challenges for so long, but looking forward to what future challenges hold for you.  That said...<br/> <br/>This looks like it has huge potential.  I hope it is in your home or a place that you can visit easily at any time.  I love the potential that this shows.  Imagine shooting through this during one of the sunsets that covers the whole sky in blood red.  Or a lighting bolt runing through the scene.  Or the moon lighting up the really dramatic whispy clouds...  See what I mean?<br/> <br/>Now take a look at what you have here.  It''s a window with some clouds.  There is nothing to hold the viewers interest.  No drama so to speak.  It''s just a window.  And it''s not shot straight.  You can tell this from the distortion of the rectangle.  So while you have a good eye for a location and have found one with some potential, it just doesn''t carry through in this image.<br/> <br/>Yours<br/>TC</td>', 'From the Critique Club: First of all, let me say welcome back!  Don''t know what kept ya out of challenges for so long, but looking forward to what future challenges hold for you.  That said... This looks like it has huge potential.  I hope it is in your home or a place that you can visit easily at any time.  I love the potential that this shows.  Imagine shooting through this during one of the sunsets that covers the whole sky in blood red.  Or a lighting bolt runing through the scene.  Or the moon lighting up the really dramatic whispy clouds...  See what I mean? Now take a look at what you have here.  It''s a window with some clouds.  There is nothing to hold the viewers interest.  No drama so to speak.  It''s just a window.  And it''s not shot straight.  You can tell this from the distortion of the rectangle.  So while you have a good eye for a location and have found one with some potential, it just doesn''t carry through in this image. YoursTC', '2006-07-11 21:37:55.000000', NULL, 0),
